IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il47-nouns`
IMPORT `il47-cross-references`

-- Row il-47. The sound citations point at what their citing words say, and the recorded facts about the defects and the controls are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- No defect is asserted sound anywhere in this file: the assertions that state what the citing words need are in il47-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in il47-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the sound citations`

-- The two controls point at what they say.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: income determination regs r 1(b), the ninth schedule`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: disabled persons income regs r 1A(1), the ninth schedule`)

§ `Tests of the second reading: the old lettering read as the new`

-- Fork R1 in NOTES.md. If a court reads the old letter as the schedule that carried it before 1995 (the schedule the Law itself marks [ב׳] on p. 301), each defect points at what its citing words say.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says if the old lettering is read as the new` (`reference: survivors pension regs r 2, item 1 of Schedule B`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says if the old lettering is read as the new` (`reference: vocational training regs r 1, item 1 of Schedule B`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says if the old lettering is read as the new` (`reference: vocational training regs r 1, item 3 of Schedule B`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says if the old lettering is read as the new` (`reference: proportional pension regs r 1(2), Schedule B`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says if the old lettering is read as the new` (`reference: grants regs r 4(a), Schedule B`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says if the old lettering is read as the new` (`reference: grants regs r 17, Schedule B`)

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- Only the survivors pension citation has both limbs from an official page image: the instrument that wrote the citing words was read.
#ASSERT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: survivors pension regs r 2, item 1 of Schedule B`)
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: vocational training regs r 1, item 1 of Schedule B`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: vocational training regs r 1, item 3 of Schedule B`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: proportional pension regs r 1(2), Schedule B`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: grants regs r 4(a), Schedule B`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: grants regs r 17, Schedule B`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: income determination regs r 1(b), the ninth schedule`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: disabled persons income regs r 1A(1), the ninth schedule`))

-- Limb (a) of every defect: the page images of the Law as enacted and of the repeal.
#ASSERT (`reference: survivors pension regs r 2, item 1 of Schedule B`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: vocational training regs r 1, item 1 of Schedule B`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: vocational training regs r 1, item 3 of Schedule B`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: proportional pension regs r 1(2), Schedule B`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: grants regs r 4(a), Schedule B`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: grants regs r 17, Schedule B`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

-- Limb (b), one by one.
#ASSERT (`reference: survivors pension regs r 2, item 1 of Schedule B`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: vocational training regs r 1, item 1 of Schedule B`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation, and the latest amending instrument read from its text layer only`
#ASSERT (`reference: vocational training regs r 1, item 3 of Schedule B`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation, and the latest amending instrument read from its text layer only`
#ASSERT (`reference: proportional pension regs r 1(2), Schedule B`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: grants regs r 4(a), Schedule B`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: grants regs r 17, Schedule B`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: income determination regs r 1(b), the ninth schedule`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: disabled persons income regs r 1A(1), the ninth schedule`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`

§ `Tests of the cited item`

-- The Treasury allocation schedule as enacted has items 1 and 2 only (SH 1522 p. 299): item 1 exists, item 3 does not.
#ASSERT (`reference: survivors pension regs r 2, item 1 of Schedule B`)'s `the cited item exists in the target as enacted` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`reference: vocational training regs r 1, item 3 of Schedule B`)'s `the cited item exists in the target as enacted` EQUALS FALSE

§ `Tests of the day the target was repealed`

-- Sefer HaChukim 2511 p. 248 item (4) repeals Schedule B; p. 249 s 31 commences it on 20 Tevet 5776 = 1 January 2016.
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: survivors pension regs r 2, item 1 of Schedule B`) (Date 1 1 2016) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: survivors pension regs r 2, item 1 of Schedule B`) (Date 2 1 2016) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: survivors pension regs r 2, item 1 of Schedule B`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: vocational training regs r 1, item 3 of Schedule B`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The day before: no source held says on which day the schedule was added, or that it stood on a given day before the repeal, so NOTHING (fork D1 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: survivors pension regs r 2, item 1 of Schedule B`) (Date 31 12 2015) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: survivors pension regs r 2, item 1 of Schedule B`) (Date 6 8 1995) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A control has no recorded repeal: NOTHING on any day, which is not a statement that its target stands.
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: income determination regs r 1(b), the ninth schedule`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: disabled persons income regs r 1A(1), the ninth schedule`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
